From: VyOS SRX build <noreply@localhost>
Subject: meson: configure checks without running target binaries

meson.build ran ~20 small test programs with cpp.run(). A cross build can only
execute them through an exe_wrapper (qemu-user or binfmt), which is slow, needs
privileges and is unavailable in unprivileged build containers.

Turn them into link/compile checks (cpp.links, cpp.compiles) or preprocessor
defines (cpp.get_define); every probe only reported success of compiling or
linking, or printed a version macro. The ClusterFuzzLite probe tested the
environment at run time: test it at configure time instead. Do not fetch the
googletest wrap unless tests or fuzzing are enabled.

Native builds get the same results.

